  "summary": {
    "plain": "Prototype lithium-molybdate detectors for AMoRE-II reached energy resolutions of 7.55 to 8.82 keV at 2.615 MeV and separated alpha particles from other events, even at temperatures as high as 30 mK.",
    "technical": "Baseline AMoRE-II module design: Li2 100MoO4 crystals of 316 g and 517-521 g operated at 10 mK; alpha discrimination power 12.37-19.50 around the 6Li(n,alpha)3H Q-value of 4.785 MeV (Eur. Phys. J. C 85, 172 (2025))."
  },
